{{/*
Shared fragments of the generated GitHub Actions workflows.

privateModulesAccess renders the pair of job steps that let a job fetch Go
modules that are not served by the module proxy: the credential rewrite that
makes git send the token to github.com, and GOPRIVATE, which is what sends
those fetches to git in the first place.

The two steps are one block on purpose. GOPRIVATE always covers
github.com/Educentr (the generated Makefile sets it the same way), so turning
it on takes every Educentr module off proxy.golang.org and onto a direct git
fetch — which is exactly the fetch the credential rewrite serves. Setting one
without the other is never what a job wants, so there is nothing to render
separately.

Call it with the root context ($): the goat-tests jobs are rendered inside a
range over the applications, where "." is one application and the fragment
would render empty.

The body deliberately starts with a newline and ends without one, so that
`{{ template "privateModulesAccess" $ }}` on a line of its own renders the
block separated from the step above by a blank line, as the steps of these
workflows are. The define tag therefore must not be trimmed with `-}}`: that
would also eat the indentation of the first step, which YAML needs.
*/}}
{{- define "privateModulesAccess" }}
      - name: Configure Git for private repos
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{"{{"}} secrets.{{ .PrivateReposTokenSecretName }} {{"}}"}}
        run: |
          git config --global url."https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/".insteadOf "https://github.com/"

      - name: Set GOPRIVATE
        run: |
          go env -w GOPRIVATE="github.com/Educentr{{ if .PrivateRepos }},{{ .PrivateRepos }}{{ end }}"
{{- end }}
